# Local runtime data
#
# ANCHORED (leading slash) on purpose. A bare `storage/` matches at every depth,
# which silently swallowed `backend/app/storage/` - the storage provider package
# imported by the routers, the worker and the seeder. Local builds kept working
# because `docker build` copies the working tree including untracked files;
# CI's `actions/checkout` gets only tracked files, so every published image was
# missing the package and crashed at boot with ModuleNotFoundError. Nothing
# failed locally, no test caught it, and the image looked like it built fine.
/storage/
/backend/storage/
/data/
*.sqlite3
*.db

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
